## Context
In raid f7fa41 (2026-10-28), gaze run by a team-lead subagent recorded `seats:
self-only` three times on PR #1915 (one cross-family seat refused) and reached
`panel` only with a same-family seat. The landing-path PRs merged with no
cross-family review, and a later cross-family pass from the interface session
found 2 blocking and 1 high regressions (see the fix ticket filed with this one).
Consent is not the cause: `~/.config/harness/gaze-seats.json` declares
cross-family spend for OpenAI and Mistral, and the same `gaze_seat.py launch
--runtime codex` works from the interface session. Cause not established:
candidates are the subagent permission layer refusing the headless `codex exec`,
nesting depth (`CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_SUBAGENT_SPAWN_DEPTH`), or the seat's sandbox
from a nested cwd.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Reproduce: one gaze from a subagent (depth 1 and 2) that plans a codex seat; record exactly what refuses it
- [ ] Fix, or a documented route: gaze from a subagent reaches a cross-family seat, or the raid escalates such PRs to a seat launched by the interface session
- [ ] verify-gate does not admit a landing-path PR whose review has no cross-family seat when one was required (`skills/route/references/decorrelation.md`)

## Raid f642df annotation (Imagine + Blind-Spot + Plan, 2026-10-28)
Premise holds: nothing merged since creation touches the surfaces.
`skills/raid/references/detached-gaze.md` substitutes a detached session when
inline gaze fails but does not route a seat to the interface session.
Drift guard: PASS (no criterion added or dropped; the notes below are inputs).

Findings to carry:
- Read raid f7fa41 artefacts first (PR #1915 gaze answers on notes, seat
  reports, plan header): `--no-cross-family` escape, `NOT-RUN:`/timeout
  report, or a refusal text. They may settle the cause before any repro.
- verify-gate has no cross-family check today (`skills/verify-gate/SKILL.md`
  § Review evidence; `scripts/review_evidence.py` computes families but
  refuses nothing). Its inputs are missing: the decorrelation risk row is an
  orchestrator judgement never recorded; producer family is not on notes;
  `--family` defaults to `unknown`; `--no-cross-family` lives in the plan
  header. Decide where the "cross-family required" signal is recorded (reuse
  the plan's consent/deviation line before inventing metadata) and key the
  check on report family, never on runtime (Claude Code, Codex, Pi alike).
- The check sits after the `review_evidence: legacy` branch and skips the
  bookkeeping tier, so in-flight PRs are not retroactively blocked.
- Bootstrap: this fix PR is itself high-risk; if hunt's gaze from a subagent
  cannot reach the codex seat, report it and the raid launches that seat from
  the interface session.
- YAGNI: no nesting-aware launcher before the cause is named; no new
  "landing-path" classifier. No overlap with 1327 (avoid editing panel.md).

Actions:
1. Read f7fa41 artefacts; then repro `gaze_seat.py launch --runtime codex`
